# Runtime state is mounted, never baked in — and it is the largest thing in the
# checkout (MariaDB data, NPM's /data, certificate material, backups). Excluding
# it keeps the build context small and makes it impossible to ship a deployment's
# live edge state inside an image.
data/
mysql/
letsencrypt/
backups/

# Dependencies and build output: the image installs and builds its own.
# `**/` matters in Docker's matcher — a bare `node_modules/` only matches the
# context root, so the per-package trees were still being sent and then baked
# into the runtime image by `COPY backend /app` (673 MB of build context instead
# of 5 MB, and dependencies the image is about to install anyway).
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
frontend/src/locale/lang/
**/node_modules/.cache/

# Repo metadata and local noise.
.git/
.gitignore
.githooks/
.github/
.build-sso.log
**/.DS_Store

# The compose files are the deploy surface, not image content.
docker-compose*.yml
compose*.yml
